>> title: Gingerbread Cookies
>> category: Cookies
>> tags: ginger, molasses, spice, christmas, oven
>> servings: 36
>> time: 2 hours
>> step.3: beat in
>> step.7: roll 1/4 in thick, cut out, bake 350°F (175°C) 10 min

Heat the #oven{} to 350°F (175°C) and line two #baking sheets{} with parchment.

Cream @unsalted butter{3/4%cup}(170 g; softened) with @dark brown sugar{3/4%cup}(165 g).

Beat @molasses{2/3%cup}(200 g), @egg{1%large}(50 g), and @vanilla extract{1%tsp}(5 mL) into @&(~1)creamed butter{}.

Whisk @all-purpose flour{3 1/2%cup}(440 g), @ground ginger{1%Tbs}(6 g), @ground cinnamon{2%tsp}(5 g), @ground cloves{1/2%tsp}(1 g), @baking soda{1%tsp}(6 g), and @table salt{1/2%tsp}(3 g).

Stir @&(~1)dry ingredients{} into @&(~2)batter{}.

Wrap @&(~1)dough{} and chill for ~{1%hour}.

Roll @&(~1)dough{} 1/4 in thick, cut out shapes, and bake at 350°F for ~{10%min}.
